+      "text": "This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent\n\nThe initial user instruction was:\n\n“[You are Servex agent task-mastermind-line-filter-gpt.]\nLoad the `sub-mastermind` and `page` skills, then: You are task-mastermind-line-filter-gpt, running on an OpenRouter model as a live test. Load the sub-mastermind skill. Your brief is public/framework/ai/2026-10-01/line-filter/requirements.md: build the line map first. Work yourself (no minions). Take a pool worktree (take_worktree) or wait for one, build /imagine/lines/, land through merge.mjs, then report to vscode-mastermind and stop.”\n\nThe requirements specify:\n- Accept any image through upload/drop or samples.\n- Produce mostly white grayscale line art: darker means greater line confidence.\n- Combine hue/saturation/brightness derivatives, structure-tensor direction coherence, continuity along the line, and signal relative to local noise.\n- Show original and result side by side, stacked on mobile.\n- Four live sliders: window size, line length, noise floor, gamma.\n- Three or four samples, including a synthetic box/room and a real photo already in the repo.\n- Keep the core pure: `lines(imageData, opts) → Float32Array`, separate from the browser UI and usable in Node.\n- Plain JavaScript and canvas ImageData; no npm packages.\n- Link from the blog post’s “Next” section and Imagine’s tools/labs navigation.\n- Land the line map FIRST. Corner map, connecting corners, SVG comparison/export, and 3D are later tasks.\n\nThe brief says Sonnet, but the explicit live-test instruction and actual session identify this builder as `openai/gpt-6.1-sol` through OpenRouter. No build minions were used. One required documentation-only reviewer was spawned.\n\nThe most recent user request is solely to summarize the conversation, in text only, without any tools.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts and Constraints\n\nProject architecture:\n- Lew42 is a no-build, static-production, native-ESM framework.\n- Browser imports use real `.js` URLs.\n- `Server/` is development-only.\n- Pages are declared through parent navigation; filesystem crawling does not create navigation.\n- Page instances use `new Page({ meta: import.meta, content(){…} })`.\n- `render` and many other names collide with core Page/View methods.\n- Framework DOM capturing is synchronous; never create framework DOM after an `await`.\n- Stylesheets are registered with `View.stylesheet(import.meta, \"file.css\")`.\n- Every CSS rule is inside a layer; full layer order is `base, theme, site, util`.\n- Imagine is a column-page experience with a shared rail. Its `GROUPS` array supplies both rail groups and preview groups.\n- The new leaf uses `width: \"fill\"` and `index: true`.\n\nFilter:\n- RGBA is composited on white before HSV conversion.\n- Hue differences are circular and weighted by saturation to suppress meaningless achromatic hue.\n- Centered differences form per-channel gradients.\n- Gradient outer products are summed across channels.\n- Square-window tensor averaging uses summed-area tables, making each tensor window constant-time.\n- Tensor coherence is eigenvalue gap / trace.\n- Gradient orientation gives the line tangent.\n- Along-tangent sampling rewards aligned direction and sustained relative magnitude.\n- Local incoherent tensor energy serves as a noise estimate.\n- Confidence is bounded to [0,1].\n- Gamma affects display only:\n  `grey = 255 * (1 - confidence ** gamma)`.\n- Interactive images are resized to a maximum 640-pixel long edge; the pure core has no resize restriction.\n- This first version computes on the main thread; worker/batch improvements are documented, not implemented.\n\nImportant instructions to preserve:\n- “Don't write my name into anything. Not in docs, readmes, skills, code, comments, commit messages, logs, or memory notes — and don't address me by it in chat. Talk to me as you; refer to me in files as you (readme voice) or the owner; a rule about who decides is ‘ask first’, not a name.”\n- “Do not edit [CLAUDE.md] without asking.”\n- Ask before breaking no-build, static-runtime, or no-new-dependency constraints.\n- “Merge carefully, never clobber.”\n- “Never link a worktree's node_modules to the main tree's.”\n- “Never force-push, and never rewrite history.”\n- Every process spawn must be hidden (`windowsHide: true`).\n- Do not drive the owner’s live browser tabs. Use headless Playwright or `mcp__site__shot`.\n- Do not discard uncommitted or unmerged work.\n- Do not edit shared skills; recommendations go to the Servex mastermind.\n- Hold live reloads before batches of live-loaded writes.\n- Cards are the owner-facing reporting surface; detailed state belongs in task logs/docs.\n- The user explicitly ordered this task to work itself, with no minions.\n- Commit attribution:\n  `Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>`\n\n3. Files and Code Sections\n\nWorking locations and IDs:\n- Main repo: `C:/Code/lew42/monorepo`\n- Pool worktree: `C:/Code/lew42/worktrees/qf-4`\n- Branch: `worktree/qf-4`\n- Worktree server: `http://127.0.0.1:59352/`\n- Agent: `task-mastermind-line-filter-gpt`\n- Session UUID: `29eacca5-0c7f-45a2-878c-c9c08722a004`\n- Task directory in MAIN:\n  `public/framework/ai/2026-10-01/line-filter`\n- Owner card:\n  `2026/10/01/line-art-from-any-image`\n- Card URL returned:\n  `/framework/ai/2026/10/01/line-art-from-any-image/`\n- Scratchpad:\n  `C:/Users/mike/.claude/projects/C--Code-lew42-monorepo/29eacca5-0c7f-45a2-878c-c9c08722a004/scratchpad/`\n\nRead:\n- Task `requirements.md` and `owner-words.md`.\n- Root/module readme chains through `load_module`:\n  - `public/imagine`\n  - `public/framework/design`\n  - design layout/content/ui/color/navigation children\n  - `public/framework/code` patterns/dos-and-donts/objects/css\n  - blog and `public/blog/ai/lines-to-3d`\n- `public/imagine/page.js`\n- `public/imagine/readme.md`\n- `public/imagine/stream/page.js`\n- `public/imagine/stream/doc/page.js`\n- `public/app.js`\n- `Server/doc/review.md`\n- `Server/layout-check.mjs` header\n- `Server/smoke.mjs` header and arguments\n- `Server/browser.mjs`\n- `public/framework/design/content/questions.md`\n- Existing photo `public/edric/image/seagul.jpeg` (480×639 paving stones and gull).\n\nCreated in WORKTREE:\n\nA. `public/imagine/lines/lines.js`\n\nSignature:\n`export function lines(image, opts = {})`\n\nInput validation:\n```\nconst { width: w, height: h, data } = image;\nif (!Number.isInteger(w) || !Number.isInteger(h) ||\n    w < 1 || h < 1 || data.length !== w * h * 4)\n    throw new TypeError(\"Expected RGBA ImageData with positive integer dimensions.\");\n```\n\nDefaults/clamps:\n```\nconst radius = Math.round(clamp(opts.window ?? 5, 3, 21) / 2 - 0.5);\nconst length = Math.round(clamp(opts.length ?? 17, 3, 61) / 2);\nconst floor = clamp(opts.noise ?? 0.006, 0.0001, 1);\n```\n\nIt creates HSV Float32Arrays, tensor arrays (`xx`, `xy`, `yy`), and magnitude.\nFor every pixel:\n```\nconst hx = circular(hue[r] - hue[l]) * Math.min(sat[l], sat[r]);\nconst hy = circular(hue[b] - hue[t]) * Math.min(sat[t], sat[b]);\nconst sx = (sat[r] - sat[l]) / 2;\nconst sy = (sat[b] - sat[t]) / 2;\nconst vx = (val[r] - val[l]) / 2;\nconst vy = (val[b] - val[t]) / 2;\nxx[i] = hx * hx + sx * sx + vx * vx;\nxy[i] = hx * hy + sx * sy + vx * vy;\nyy[i] = hy * hy + sy * sy + vy * vy;\nmag[i] = Math.sqrt(xx[i] + yy[i]);\n```\n\nTensor and response:\n```\nconst trace = a[i] + c[i];\nconst gap = Math.hypot(a[i] - c[i], 2 * b[i]);\ncoherence[i] = trace > 1e-12 ? Math.min(1, gap / trace) : 0;\nangle[i] = Math.atan2(2 * b[i], a[i] - c[i]) / 2;\nconst noise = Math.sqrt(Math.max(0, trace - gap));\nresponse[i] = mag[i] / (mag[i] + floor + noise);\n```\n\nContinuity samples along `(-sin(angle), cos(angle))`, rounds sample positions, skips out-of-image points, and uses:\n```\nconst aligned = Math.max(0, Math.cos(2 * (angle[j] - angle[i])));\nsupport += coherence[j] * aligned * Math.min(1, mag[j] / mag[i]);\nresult[i] = coherence[i] * response[i] * (count ? support / count : 0);\n```\n\nHelpers:\n- `circular(value)` wraps to [-0.5,0.5).\n- `clamp(value,min,max)` accepts finite numeric conversions.\n- `average(values,w,h,radius)` uses Float64 summed-area tables and returns Float32 averages.\n\nB. `public/imagine/lines/page.js`\n\nComplete page shape:\n```\nimport { Page, View, div, p, a } from \"/app.js\";\nimport { mount } from \"./tool.js\";\nView.stylesheet(import.meta, \"lines.css\");\n\nexport default new Page({\n    meta: import.meta,\n    title: \"Line art\",\n    description: \"Turn any image into line art: darker pixels mark steadier, straighter edges.\",\n    icon: \"gesture\",\n    width: \"fill\",\n    index: true,\n    content(){\n        p(\"Darker means more likely to be a line. Drop an image or try a sample.\");\n        const host = div.c(\"lines-tool\");\n        mount(host.el);\n        a(\"How the filter works\").href(\"./doc/filter/\");\n    },\n});\n```\nA comment records sizing: Imagine column row, fill remaining width, two panes stacked at 400 and beside each other at 1200+, controls above and one doc link below.\nNo page_work widget was added.\n\nC. `public/imagine/lines/tool.js`\n\n`export function mount(host)`:\n- Fixed internal HTML for:\n  - Sample select: box, faint seam + noise, room, photo.\n  - File picker (`accept=\"image/*\"`).\n  - Save PNG button.\n  - Four sliders.\n  - Original and result canvases.\n  - Live status.\n- Slider ranges:\n  - Window 3–21, step 2, default 5.\n  - Length 3–61, step 2, default 17.\n  - Noise 0.001–0.05, step 0.001, default 0.006.\n  - Gamma 0.2–2, step 0.05, default 0.8.\n- Debounces core calculation for 60 ms.\n- Gamma repaints without rerunning core.\n- Displays dimensions and measured milliseconds.\n- `show(image)` resizes at most 640 long edge, paints white behind alpha, reads ImageData.\n- Image decoding uses a generation token so stale async loads cannot overwrite later selections.\n- Photo URL:\n  `new URL('../../edric/image/seagul.jpeg', import.meta.url).href`\n- Upload validates image MIME, uses object URLs, revokes after decode.\n- Host supports dragover/drop.\n- PNG export uses `canvas.toBlob`, temporary anchor, object URL revoked after 1 second.\n- Browser state/images remain local.\n\nD. `public/imagine/lines/samples.js`\n\n`export function sample(name)` returns a locally drawn 560×400 canvas:\n- Box: 8 known vertices and 12 wireframe edges, including hidden edges.\n- Room: back wall, perspective connections, door/window rectangles.\n- Faint seam: grey 204/208 left/right split; lower rectangular area has deterministic random noise (LCG seed 42).\n- Photo is loaded separately by tool.js.\nSynthetic pixel colors are literals because these are image inputs, while UI CSS uses tokens.\n\nE. `public/imagine/lines/lines.css`\n- Full layer declaration; rules in `@layer site`.\n- Tool grid, bounded `max-width:90em`, centered.\n- Wrapping input row.\n- Four-column slider grid.\n- Two equal image columns.\n- Canvas width 100%, auto height, token border.\n- Under 800px: two slider columns and stacked images.\n- Uses `--gap`, `--gap-50`, `--ink`.\n- Native controls remain intentionally simple.\n\nF. `public/imagine/lines/readme.md`\n- Opens with link to live filter.\n- Pure function snippet.\n- RGBA input and Float32Array [0,1] output.\n- Gamma is display-only.\n- Test command:\n  `node public/imagine/lines/test.mjs`\n- Documents browser 640-pixel cap by link to limits.\n- Links filter doc, original blog idea, task log.\n\nG. `public/imagine/lines/doc/filter.md`\n- Three ingredients and four sliders.\n- Formula and display mapping.\n- Honest limits: confidence heuristic, not probability/object recognition; corners can lose coherence; hidden wireframe edges are known input, not detected counts.\n- Main-thread computation and interactive size limit.\n- Existing photo source.\n- Explicitly no 3D, corner detector, or SVG extraction yet.\n\nH. `public/imagine/lines/doc/page.js`\n- Plain Page.\n- Dynamic `route(\"filter\")` returns a page using:\n  `md.file(meta, \"filter.md\", { h1: false })`\n- Other names return null.\n- Index links to `/imagine/lines/doc/filter/`.\n\nI. `public/imagine/lines/test.mjs`\n- Node assertions:\n  - Constant field all zero.\n  - Faint grey seam mean >0.35.\n  - All seam values finite in [0,1].\n  - Faint seam > five times random texture mean.\n  - Hue/color edge mean >0.5.\n  - Horizontal seam >0.35.\n  - Isolated speck maximum <0.1 at length 41.\n  - 1×1 image returns zero.\n- Deterministic texture RNG.\n- Prints actual metrics.\n\nModified in WORKTREE:\n- `public/imagine/page.js`:\n  Tools GROUPS string changed from\n  `\"paging importance research stream cms generated\"`\n  to\n  `\"lines paging importance research stream cms generated\"`.\n  Existing GROUPS remains single navigation source.\n- `public/imagine/readme.md`:\n  Added a first Use item linking Line art.\n- `public/blog/ai/lines-to-3d/post.md`:\n  Replaced old Next paragraph with:\n  “[Try the line-map prototype](/imagine/lines/): drop a photo, compare the original with line art, and tune how strongly faint, steady edges show up. Corners, vectors and 3D come after this first map works.”\n- `public/blog/words.js`:\n  Generated word-count update from blog/meta.mjs.\n- `public/blog/ai/index.html` was inadvertently regenerated for unrelated drift and then restored to its pre-task version. It is NOT part of the task commits.\n\nCommits:\n- `10441d7d` — Build the first line-confidence image filter.\n- `ed7b367e` — Keep deterministic line-map checks beside the filter.\nBoth have required Claude attribution.\nNo merge yet.\n\nUnrelated pre-existing worktree edit:\n- `.claude/skills/clarity/flags.jsonl` was modified before task edits (initial status).\n- It was deliberately not staged/committed/restored.\n- This may prevent safe pool