+      "text": "This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   I am `task-mastermind-ai2-inbox-read`, a Servex sub-mastermind agent. My original assignment: load the `sub-mastermind` and `page` skills, then own the task described at `public/framework/ai/2026-09-30/ai2-inbox-read/requirements.md` (owner-words.md beside it) end-to-end. Build six things in the AI 2 Inbox (`/framework/ai2/`):\n   1. Inbox only — hide the \"Needs you\" tab (don't delete its code) — **LATER CORRECTED, see below**.\n   2. Read and unread — unread rows bold/different; opening a row marks it read; per-viewer (localStorage fine for v1).\n   3. Archive / clear — each row gets a button that removes it from the Inbox; **nothing is ever deleted**; archived items stay in the Log and on their card.\n   4. Automatic resolution — a row leaves the Inbox by itself when resolved: an ask answered (a `chose` line), a question replied to, a task landed or stopped, a card marked done. Write the resolution rule down, in one place, in a comment.\n   5. Search — one search box that finds any card or row, including archived ones, by title and text.\n   6. The Now/Live card has redundant wording (\"Running now\", then \"working\" on every row, then \"· now\" after each) — say it once: the heading says it, rows just name the agent and what it's doing.\n\n   Rules from requirements.md: Pool worktree (`take_worktree`), then `merge.mjs` with the smoke test, then the review skill. Screenshots at 400 and 1920. Budget: **$8, hard. At most 1 minion.** Post one short card when live: http://10.0.0.135:8137/framework/ai2/. Coordinate with `task-mastermind-cards-and-logs` if it touches the same files (not yet needed — no conflict surfaced).\n\n   **Mid-task owner correction** (relayed via `[from: servex-mastermind-opus]`): \"Make Needs you a FILTER inside the Inbox list (for example a chip: 'Needs you'), not a hidden tab with its own UI. Leave everything else in your brief as it is. A later task (ai/2026-09-30/inbox-ext) moves the Inbox to /framework/ai/ as a page extension and gives the Log the same UI. So keep your code easy to carry over: read state, archive and resolution rules in one small module. Usage is over pace on the 5-hour window, so stay lean.\" This explicitly supersedes ask #1's \"hide the tab\" approach, and adds a structural requirement that asks 2-4's logic live together in one small, portable module (because a future task, `ai/2026-09-30/inbox-ext`, will carry it elsewhere), plus a directive to minimize token/work spend given the 5-hour usage window is over pace.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Servex agent hierarchy: mastermind → sub-mastermind (me) → minion, spawned via `mcp__servex__spawn_agent`, coordinated via `mcp__servex__send_to_agent` (queued vs `now` priority), `mcp__servex__claim_topic` for module ownership, `mcp__servex__take_worktree`/`return_worktree` for the quick-fix worktree pool.\n   - Task logging convention: `task.jsonl` (append-only, one JSON object per line, one verb per key: `assign`, `log`, `decision`, `agent`, etc.), written via `node .claude/hooks/append.mjs <target.jsonl> <lines.json>` (lines.json written with the Write tool, never a heredoc/shell string).\n   - AI 2's architecture: a rail (list) + detail column, driven by `board(page)` in `page.js`, with data assembled by `items()` in `inbox.js` from three streamed logs (board.jsonl, Servex prompts, day.jsonl) plus Servex \"card folders\" (`CardList`). Cards can be old-style `board.jsonl` entries or new folder-based cards (`is_folder_id()` test: id starts with 4-digit year).\n   - Existing shared-rule pattern (`needs-rule.js`'s `card_needs()`): a pure function reading raw `page.jsonl` lines, shared by three consumers (Needs you tab, rail's \"Needs review\" filter, Servex's `/waiting` route) so they can never disagree — this is the pre