+      "text": "This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   I am `task-mastermind-ai2-inbox-read`, a Servex sub-mastermind agent. My assignment (established in prior, compacted context): load the `sub-mastermind` and `page` skills, then own the task at `public/framework/ai/2026-09-30/ai2-inbox-read/requirements.md` (with `owner-words.md` beside it) end-to-end. Build six things in the AI 2 Inbox (`/framework/ai2/`):\n   1. \"Needs you\" as a FILTER CHIP inside the Inbox list (not a hidden tab) — per a mid-task owner correction relayed via `[from: servex-mastermind-opus]` that explicitly superseded the original brief's \"hide the tab\" approach.\n   2. Read and unread — unread rows bold/different; **opening a row marks it read** (the brief's literal words); per-viewer (localStorage).\n   3. Archive/clear — a button on each row that removes it from the Inbox; nothing is ever deleted; archived items stay in the Log and on their card.\n   4. Automatic resolution — a row leaves the Inbox by itself when resolved (ask answered, question replied to, task landed/stopped, card marked done); the rule is written down in one place, in a comment.\n   5. Search — one search box finding any card or row, including archived ones, by title and text.\n   6. The Now/Live card's redundant wording (\"Running now\", then \"working\" on every row, then \"· now\" after each) said once.\n   Additional structural requirement from the owner correction: read/archive/resolution logic must live together in ONE small, portable module (because a future task, `ai/2026-09-30/inbox-ext`, will carry it elsewhere), plus a directive to minimize spend given the 5-hour usage window was over pace.\n   Process rules: Pool worktree (`take_worktree`), then `merge.mjs` with the smoke test, then the review skill. Screenshots at 400 and 1920. Budget: **$8, hard. At most 1 minion.** Post one short card when live: `http://10.0.0.135:8137/framework/ai2/` (original) — actual live reachable at `http://monorepo.localhost/framework/ai2/`. Coordinate with other tasks touching the same files if overlap surfaces.\n   No further explicit human/owner instructions arrived during this segment of the conversation — all \"messages\" received were Servex inter-agent relays (the minion's status reports, and `mastermind-servex-9`'s file-overlap notice), which I addressed per the established Servex coordination protocol, not because a human directed me to in this segment.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Servex agent hierarchy and tools: `mcp__servex__spawn_agent`, `send_to_agent`, `claim_topic`/`release_topic`, `take_worktree`/`return_worktree`, `heartbeat_status`, `stop_agent`, `ListAgents`/`SendMessage` for cross-session coordination.\n   - Task logging convention: `task.jsonl` append-only via `node .claude/hooks/append.mjs <target.jsonl> <lines.json>` (lines.json always written with the Write tool, never inline shell strings — shell backtick-eating is a documented hazard).\n   - `merge.mjs` review gate: a worktree branch must have a FRESH review (`node Server/review.mjs <taskdir> <worktree>`) with every `[fix]` finding answered (`{\"review\":{\"answer\":{\"n\":N,\"reply\":\"fixed: .../declined: .../noted: ...\"}}}}` appended to task.jsonl, then `node Server/review.mjs --turns <taskdir>` to mirror answers into `review.jsonl`); a \"declined\" answer spawns a fresh second reviewer (phase 3) to accept/reject the decline. `merge.mjs` applies the branch diff into the MAIN TREE's WORKING DIRECTORY uncommitted (\"the owner commits\") — three-way merges union-append jsonl files, takes the branch's version of code files unchanged in main, and refuses on real content conflicts.\n   - `git-guard.mjs` PreToolUse hook: blocks `git checkout -- <path>` and `git restore` unconditionally with the message \"blocked in the main checkout... commit your files by path instead\" — appears to fire even inside a genuine separate git worktree, not just the shared main checkout; no confirmed workaround found other than committing instead of discarding.\n   - `review.mjs`'s finding/answer/reply lifecycle: phase 1 (findings, kind `\"fix\"` or `\"note\"`), phase 2 (answers: `fixed`/`declined`/`noted` prefixes, matched by regex), phase 3 (only for unanswered declines — a fresh reviewer replies `accept`/reject with `stance`).\n   - `node Server/text-check.mjs <taskdir>`: flags outcome paragraphs over 60 words, outcomes over 120 words total, and other prose-heavy files with no picture. The `finish-task` skill instructs appending a SHORTER landing line when flagged (the latest `assign` line \"wins\").\n   - `public/framework/ai/asks.jsonl`: an append-only ledger of routed owner asks; `Servex/asks/mark.mjs` is referenced by the `finish-task` skill as the tool to mark an ask landed but **does not exist** (`MODULE_NOT_FOUND` confirmed) — worked around by hand-appending a `status: \"landed\"` line in the same shape as the existing entry.\n   - Usage/budget: `check-claude-usage` skill → `python $env:USERPROFILE\\.claude\\bin\\claude-usage.py --json`. Confirmed at task-closing time: **session (5h) window 72%** (up from 61% at task start), **weekly_all 91%, severity \"critical\"**. This directly supports the \"stay lean\" directive and my decision to skip further optional quality-assurance steps.\n   - `rules.js` module pattern: one small file holding `is_read`/`mark_read` (localStorage key `\"ai2-read-ids\"`), `archive_row(it)`, and `is_resolved(it)` — explicitly built this way per the owner's mid-task correction so a future task (`inbox-ext`) can carry it elsewhere wholesale.\n   - `mcp__site__shot(url, width, height)`: headless screenshot tool used for my own independent visual verification (never trusting the minion's word), at both the isolated worktree dev server (`http://127.0.0.1:52373/`) and the real live site (`http://monorepo.localhost/`).\n   - Sub-mastermind principle reinforced: \"Mastermind decides, never asks\" — no approval gates sought for any judgment call in this segment (fixing bugs directly, declining findings, skipping optional review steps, not returning the worktree).\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **`public/framework/ai2/rules.js`** (new file, in worktree `qf-9`, then merged to `michael/dev`) — the one consolidated module for read/unread, archive, and automatic resolution. Final state after my fixes:\n     ```js\n     import { archive_card, append_card, is_folder_id } from \"./inbox.js\";\n     import { needs_for } from \"./needs.js\";\n\n     const READ_KEY = \"ai2-read-ids\";\n     function read_set(){ try { return new Set(JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(READ_KEY) ?? \"[]\")); } catch { return new Set(); } }\n     function save_read(set){ try { localStorage.setItem(READ_KEY, JSON.stringify([...set])); } catch {} }\n     export function is_read(id){ return read_set().has(id); }\n     export function mark_read(id, val = true){\n         const set = read_set();\n         val ? set.add(id) : set.delete(id);\n         save_read(set);\n     }\n\n     export async function archive_row(it){\n         return is_folder_id(it.id) ? append_card(it.id, { status: \"archived\", by: \"owner\" }) : archive_card(it.id);\n     }\n\n     export function is_resolved(it){\n         if (it.kind === \"live\" || it.status === \"archived\") return false;\n         if (it.status === \"done\") return true;\n         if (it.kind === \"landed\") return true;\n         if (it.kind !== \"card\" || ![\"question\", \"task\"].includes(it.type)) return false;\n         return needs_for(it.id).length === 0;\n     }\n     ```\n     I rewrote `is_resolved()` (originally just `needs_for(it.id).length === 0`, which the review correctly flagged as over-broad — dimming nearly every row since cards that never had an ask also trivially satisfy \"nothing open\") and updated the read/unread section's header comment to reflect that opening a card now DOES mark read (correcting a misattribution to the old, different 2026-09-22 \"never auto-mark read\" decision).\n   - **`public/framework/ai2/page.js`** — central UI file, multiple edits:\n     - `visible()`: added `base = base.filter(it => !is_resolved(it));` (resolved rows now actually leave the Inbox, not just dim); search now always includes archived cards when `search_q` is set, regardless of the `show_archived` toggle:\n       ```js\n       const archived = (list.archived ?? []).filter(it => !groups.filed(it));\n       if (search_q){\n           const hit = it => (it.title + \" \" + (it.text ?? \"\")).toLowerCase().includes(search_q);\n           return [...base.filter(hit), ...archived.filter(hit)];\n       }\n       return show_archived ? [...base, ...archived] : base;\n       ```\n     - `watch_needs(...)` handler: added a `last_needs_ids` closure variable and early-return when the sorted id-set string hasn't changed, to stop repainting the whole rail on every poll tick.\n     - `refill()`: removed the dead `rec.$row.el.classList.toggle(\"ai2-resolved\", ...)` line (no longer reachable since resolved rows are filtered out of the list entirely).\n     - `open()`'s doc comment: rewrote the stale \"⚠ OPENING A CARD MARKS NOTHING\" warning to correctly distinguish the OLD (different, shared, 2026-09-22) decision from the NEW (per-browser, ask-2-literal) \"opening a row marks it read\" behavior.\n     - (From the minion's original build, verified correct): the \"Needs you\" tab-strip entry removed; the rail's \"Needs review\" checkbox relabelled \"Needs you\" and given the count badge (`$needs_count`); a search `<input>` added to the chrome row; `row_on(rec, it)` helper providing `toggle_read()`/`archive()` callbacks threaded into `row(it, on)`.\n   - **`public/framework/ai2/card.js`** — added `import { mark_read } from \"./rules.js\";` and, in `activated()`:\n     ```js\n     activated(){\n         this.seen_from = null;