+      "text": "This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   I was spawned as Servex agent `task-mastermind-inspect` with the instruction: \"Load the `sub-mastermind` and `page` skills, then: You are task-mastermind-inspect. Load the sub-mastermind skill. Your brief is public/framework/ai/2026-10-01/inspect/requirements.md, with owner-words.md beside it. Part 1 (inspect() and static icon, built on ux/Content/Object) lands first. Then Part 2: the Dictate playground as a full-bleed, live system diagram. Use at most 2 Sonnet minions. Report each landing to vscode-mastermind.\"\n\n   The owner's underlying ask (recovered verbatim from a deleted brief — see below) is, in summary: give every class an icon (`static icon`) and a built-in `inspect()` view (separate from `render()`) that shows an instance's or class's structure as a card — icon, name, properties, methods, with nested object/array properties recursively shown as their own nested cards. Use this as the foundation to rebuild the `/framework/ux/Dictate/playground/` page as a full-bleed (`classes: \"full\"`), 3440-friendly, real-time 2D layout showing every real object a dictation session creates (audio source, segments, raw/clean transcriptions, prompt analysis, chat messages, session/files) as live, updating `inspect()` cards — append-only/immutable, never reordering, with the raw transcription always staying visible after cleanup.\n\n   Constraints explicitly given: at most 2 Sonnet minions total; Part 1 must land before Part 2 starts; report each landing (interpreted as: post to the owner's dashboard card, since \"vscode-mastermind\" resolves to the owner's own VS Code session, not a reachable Servex agent); coordinate with the sibling task `@task-mastermind-one-dictation` (which owns the live Dictate chat widget) so Part 2 builds a diagram around that widget, not a second one.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Lew42 framework conventions: no-build native ESM, `assign`-based OOP constructors, \"parts as statics\" (`Thing.View = class extends DefaultView`), one-function-per-concept modules (`object()`, `view()`, now `inspect()`), CSS must live in `@layer` (`base theme site util`), CSS class naming must follow module-prefix conventions (`ux-content-object-*`, `ux-content-inspect-*`).\n   - The `ux/Content/Object` module's existing two views: `object()` (small summary card) and `view()`/`DefaultView` (lazy expandable tree of `ui/item` rows, with cycle-guarding via a `path` Set of ancestors).\n   - `code/objects` pattern: \"every class ships a view of its state\" at three sizes (chip/row/panel) — `inspect()` is framed as the 4th size (the debug view).\n   - Page layout system: `classes: \"standard\"` (default, measured column) vs `classes: \"full\"` (full-bleed); `core/Layout` has 30 named arrangements; the `layout` skill's sizing questions.\n   - Servex multi-agent orchestration: `spawn_agent` with `task: {dir, parent_task, card, brief, after}` auto-opens a child's task.jsonl; `claim_topic`/`list_claims` for coordination; the spawn-gate RAM queue (threshold ~4096MB free); `parent`-linked agents auto-wake their parent on completion (no polling needed); `stop_agent` to free RAM after reading a result (keeps it resumable).\n   - `node Server/merge.mjs <worktree> [pages]`: runs a smoke test against the main tree's own `smoke.mjs`, reads a review gate off `task.jsonl`/review files on the MAIN tree's disk (not the worktree's), and performs a three-way merge if the main tree has uncommitted edits in touched paths.\n   - The sub-mastermind discipline: never write code/CSS by hand (minions only, with a narrow one-turn-piece exception for dequeuing); always verify a landed minion's work with fresh, independent evidence (read real diffs, take own screenshots via `mcp__site__shot`, don't trust the report alone); judge each delivera